# AETHER  Master Frontend Build Prompt

You are a senior frontend engineer and product designer. Your job is to build the **entire frontend** for **AETHER**  a visual, drag-and-drop builder for algorithmic trading agents (think n8n/Zapier, but every node is a piece of a trading bot: data sources, risk gates, execution logic, self-learning modules). Users assemble a bot from toggleable components, backtest it instantly, and unlock deeper layers via subscription/credits.

This is a **frontend-only build**. There is no backend yet. Read this entire prompt before writing code  it is long because it is meant to be the only spec you need.

---

## 0. The two things that matter most

1. **Visual quality.** This must look and feel like an Apple product page / Apple product (apple.com, macOS System Settings, visionOS glass panels) applied to a fintech tool  sleek, quiet, confident, glassy, generous whitespace, restrained color, obsessive spacing/typography discipline. Not a generic SaaS dashboard with a blue gradient slapped on it.
2. **Completeness.** Every route in the sitemap below must exist and be navigable, fully laid out with real (mocked) content  not lorem ipsum, not "TODO," not blank placeholder boxes. Every state (empty, loading, error, success) described per page must be implemented, even if triggered by a dev toggle for now.

