## 1. Ground rules (read this twice)

- **You cannot do any real functionality yet**  no real auth, no real database, no real payments, no real ML/backtesting compute, no real market data, no real websockets to an exchange. **Everything is mocked.** Section 9 tells you exactly how.
- Every button, form, and flow must still be **fully wired up on the frontend**  clicking "Run Backtest" should trigger a fake progress bar and then render a fully populated (fake, but realistic) results dashboard. Nothing should be a dead end or a console.log with no visual result.
- Build every page as a **real route** in the router, not a Figma-style static mockup. Navigation between all pages must actually work.
- Where a page needs auth state (logged in vs out, plan tier, onboarding complete), fake that state with a simple global store (see §9) and add a small dev-only switcher (a floating panel, hidden behind a keyboard shortcut like `Ctrl+Shift+D`) to toggle: logged in/out, plan (Free/Starter/Pro), onboarding complete, dark/light. This is your own tool for building and demoing  make it, but keep it visually out of the way.
- Do not invent new pages beyond what's listed. Do not skip pages either. If something is ambiguous, make the most Apple-like, most polished choice and move on  don't ask, just build.

