### 7.10 Builder / Canvas  "The Loom" (`/app/builder/new`, `/app/builder/:botId`, `/app/builder/:botId/version/:versionId`)
**This is the centerpiece page  spend the most effort here.** Build on React Flow.

**Toolbar** (top, glass bar): editable bot name (inline text edit) · Save · "Save as Preset ▾" dropdown (new/update existing) · Version history dropdown (preview + Restore) · Undo/Redo · Validate · Templates (quick-insert common sub-graphs) · Share (link + visibility) · **Run Backtest** (primary pill button) · Go Live (secondary, gated/locked style if plan doesn't allow) · zoom controls (+/−/fit-to-screen/% readout).

**Left panel  Component Library**: search box, category tabs/accordion for all 12 layers (Data Collection, Feature Engineering, Intelligence Agents, ML Prediction, Reinforcement Learning, Debate Layer, Confidence Engine, Risk Management, Execution, Trade Monitoring, Self-Learning, Memory). Each entry: draggable glass card with icon, name, one-liner, lock badge + unlock price if gated. Hover shows a tooltip with fuller description, inputs/outputs, "Learn more →" link to `/app/library/:componentId`. Dragging a card onto the canvas instantiates a node that auto-snaps into its correct layer band.

**Center  Canvas** (React Flow): infinite pan (space+drag, middle-mouse, two-finger scroll) / zoom (scroll/pinch), grid background with snap-to-grid toggle, minimap bottom-right (click-to-jump), marquee + shift-click multi-select with group move/delete/disable, snap guides + Align/Distribute toolbar on multi-select.

- **Layer bands**: colored, translucent horizontal bands behind grouped nodes, each labeled ("LAYER I  DATA COLLECTION," etc.), auto-expanding to fit contents, collapsible (click label → compact chip "3 nodes, 2 enabled"). Matching "Layer visibility" checklist in the left sidebar to toggle whole bands.
- **Node anatomy**: icon + name + layer-color accent border, input ports left / output ports right (color-coded by type: `MarketData`, `NewsFeed`, `FeatureVector`, `Signal`, `RiskDecision`, `ExecutionOrder`, `TradeOutcome`), on/off toggle switch in the header, status dot (grey=disabled, green=enabled+valid, amber=needs config, red=error), lock badge overlay replacing the toggle when gated.
- **Node states**: enabled/valid (solid border, green dot); disabled (greyed, dashed outline, dashed connections); locked (padlock overlay, click opens Unlock modal not the inspector); needs-config (amber dot + warning tooltip listing missing fields); error during a run (red pulsing border + tooltip); active during a live run (subtle pulse/glow).
- **Node interactions**: click → opens right Node Inspector; double-click → same + focuses first field; drag → move; right-click → context menu (Duplicate, Disable/Enable, Delete, View docs, Save as mini-preset); drag from a port → draw a connection.
- **Connections**: dragging from an output to a compatible input connects them; while dragging, compatible ports highlight and incompatible drops are refused with an inline toast explaining why. Mock a few structural rules (e.g. Execution can't connect directly to raw Data Collection; Self-Learning needs a Trade Monitoring input) and surface violations via the **Validate** button, which lists every problem in the bottom Console with click-to-jump links.

**Right panel  Node Inspector**: appears on node select. Name (editable), description, on/off toggle (mirrors header), all config fields for that node type (e.g. News Source: channel checkboxes, API key field, refresh interval slider; Risk Gate: threshold sliders, false-positive/negative cost weighting, max position size; Self-Learning: sub-module toggles, retraining frequency; Execution: venue/API select, order type, slippage tolerance), "Remove from canvas" (confirm if connected).

**Bottom panel  Console** (collapsible): validation warnings/errors, live log stream during a (simulated) run.

**Paywall interaction**: clicking a locked node opens an Unlock modal (glass, centered, no full-page redirect)  component name, description, price, embedded mock Razorpay checkout (§9.3). On mock success: modal closes, lock badge → normal toggle, toast "Unlocked  {component} is ready to configure." On cancel/fail: node stays locked, no interruption.

**Sub-flows**: select a connected group → "Save as mini-preset" → appears under "My saved blocks" in the library, draggable as a single unit elsewhere.

**Empty/first-time state**: light watermark hint "Drag a component from the left to get started," arrow pointing at the library. Incomplete-graph Run Backtest attempt → friendly blocking modal listing exactly what's missing.

**Keyboard shortcuts**: Delete (remove selected), Cmd/Ctrl+D (duplicate), Cmd/Ctrl+Z / Shift+Z (undo/redo), Cmd/Ctrl+S (save), Space+drag (pan). Autosave + a visible "unsaved changes" indicator + a browser-navigation guard.

